WEBVTT

00:00:00.444 --> 00:00:03.667
Sometimes a direct cast is sufficient.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:10.487
If the text is already in a clear date format that PostgreSQL recognizes and you have validated the input,

00:00:10.487 --> 00:00:12.897
casting to date can be simple.

00:00:12.897 --> 00:00:18.052
When the format is different, TO_DATE lets you specify the pattern.

00:00:18.052 --> 00:00:24.302
For mixed raw input, first identify the shape and then apply the appropriate parser.

00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:29.697
Blindly parsing unknown text can cause errors or incorrect interpretations.

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:36.847
Parsing converts text into a typed value; formatting converts a typed value into presentation text.

00:00:36.847 --> 00:00:43.217
Perform analytical work on typed dates and timestamps, then format near the presentation layer.

00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:49.552
If parsing can fail, validate the incoming pattern first instead of letting one malformed value stop an entire

00:00:49.552 --> 00:00:50.560
load.
